  "title": "An exact six-period correction to the printed elliptic billiard assertion k108",
  "description": "<p>Two strictly convex primitive six-period billiard trajectories in x\u00b2/4+y\u00b2=1, sharing a nondegenerate confocal elliptical caustic, give exact unequal values 11664/3125 and 3645/1024 for the literal k108 quotient in Table 2 of Reznik\u2013Garcia\u2013Koiller (arXiv:2004.12497v11 and the 2021 journal version). The horizontal coordinates and caustic are explicitly credited to Garcia\u2013Reznik, arXiv:2011.06640v1, Appendix B.5.1 (12 November 2020), and its 2022 published successor. Connected family and symmetry machinery are credited to Stachel. This is an attributed corrective application, not new six-period geometry or a claimed all-period repair. Historical firstness and independent discovery are unconfirmed.</p><p>AI tools were used extensively in mathematical development, source comparison, drafting, reproduction and adversarial checking. This research note is unrefereed and has not undergone conventional human peer review. Exact diagnostics support the written proof and are not proof-assistant formalization. The accompanying source and exact verification package permit independent reproduction of the stated certificates. The historical search is bounded and does not establish exclusive priority.</p>",
